{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Is it for HaShem that you requite this?</b> After He intended to make you supreme above all the nations in place of a kingdom of priests — is it truly fitting that you requite Him this: that you frustrate His design to profane His holy name and prevent Him from attaining the end that He intended in saying, נַעֲשֶׂה אָדָם בְּצַלְמֵנוּ כִּדְמוּתֵנוּ (Genesis 1:26)?" "<b>A foolish nation.</b> Contemptible, in that you are ungrateful and repay evil for good to your Benefactor — the opposite of the noble and honored generous man, who does good even to one who has never done him good." "<b>And not wise.</b> In practical judgment, to understand the ultimate outcome of a matter — what the result will be." "<b>Is He not your Father, who acquired you?</b> Not a natural father, who gives some form of existence by chance, but a deliberate Father, who gave you existence in order that you be His acquired possession, prepared to attain in you His desire and chosen treasure. And this is because He made you into a nation — for you were not reckoned a nation at all." "<b>And established you.</b> He gave you preparations whereby you would be prepared to become His treasured nation."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The lemma cites the verse with a heterodox apostrophe-like form of the divine name; normalized here to HaShem per the standard transliteration rules for reverent abbreviations."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:57.684380082Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}